  "slug": "archaea-duplication-d927",
  "summary": "Foundation models and multi-scale haplotype methods now extend cross-genome comparison to repeats, selection signatures, and structural variants.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread across these items is inference of functional and evolutionary consequences from sequence variation compared across accessions, isolates, and genomic scales, though the methods differ. The olive study surveys 117,119 polymorphic STRs in 212 accessions and benchmarks three plant genomic language models on embeddings responding to STR length variation. SHADES applies a multi-scale deep learning framework to haplotype variation across genomic resolutions to distinguish neutrality, sweeps, and balancing selection. The Brettanomyces graph pangenome of 1060 isolates detects 5972 structural variants, with allopolyploids carrying more SVs and hybridization-associated SVs linked to functional impact. What is new here is the pairing of repeat-level variation with foundation-model interpretation and haplotype-scale selection inference within graph and cross-genome frameworks. The items do not test a shared mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
